    },
    {
      "id": "dungeons",
      "title": "Dungeons",
      "intro_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section covers everything you can find in dungeons. You will need to complete an investigation before you can explore a dungeon. Here is the legend for the bestiary:"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Lv---Level\nArcana---Enemy's Arcana. This doesn't really affect anything in game.\nHP---Hit Points\nSP---Spirit Points\nPhy---Physical\nFir---Fire\nIce---Ice\nElc---Electricity\nWnd---Wind\nLgt---Light\nDrk---Dark\nWk---Weak\nStr---Strong/Resist\nNul---Null/Block\nRpl---Repel/Reflect\nDrn---Drain/Absorb\nRD---Rainy Day\nFloor---Floors listed are suggestions and not the only places they spawn. If the floor listed is N/A, then they are summoned by the shadow above in the list."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "persona-compendium",
      "title": "Persona Compendium",
      "intro_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section covers all information regarding Personas, including suggestions on possible fusion combinations. I've also included the formula for fusions if you need a specific Persona. Unfortunately, I can't include a fusion chart because the image is too big, so look under the section of the arcana you need for fusion combinations. For Triangle Spreads you need to calculate the resulting arcana of the first two Personas under Normal Spread and combine that with the third Persona under Triangle Spread. You may want to use Ctrl + F to help find what you need. Special Fusions have specific fusion requirements listed down below and Ultimate Personas can only be fused after maxing the Social Link of the respective arcana. Note that for both Normal and Triangle Spreads, using the same arcana in a fusion will make the resulting arcana match the one you fused with. This is a good starting point if you are having trouble fusing a Persona of a specific arcana."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "social-links",
      "title": "Social Links",
      "intro_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section covers the most complex mechanic in the game. Social Links run on a point based system. Earn enough points and you will rank up, with Rank 10 as the max. Some Social Links level up automatically, or after completing certain quests. Others require a certain rank of a Status Parameter in order to unlock. If you have a Persona of the same arcana as the Social Link you are hanging out with then you earn bonus points. In this section, when listing points the first number is if you don't have a matching Persona and the second number is if you do have a matching Persona. Just one number means it doesn't matter if you have a Persona, and a question mark means either the amount depends on the exact scenario, or I need to go back and check the amount you get. Here are points you get from any Social Link:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Spending time with a Social Link: +2 or +3"
            },
            {
              "text": "Choose responses the Social Link likes: +? (depends on response)"
            },
            {
              "text": "Have a Persona of the matching arcana: Bonus Points"
            },
            {
              "text": "Sunday hangout: +? (depends on the day)"
            },
            {
              "text": "Answer a question for a classmate: +1 or +2"
            },
            {
              "text": "Get a good score on exams: +? (depends on result)"
            },
            {
              "text": "Certain story scenes: +? (depends on the day)"
            },
            {
              "text": "Draw a relationship fortune: +? (depends on result)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Social Links that use the point system have a schedule on when they are available to spend time with. It is important to note that the schedules noted in this section are a general guideline and not set in stone. Social Link schedules can and will vary depending on a variety of things, such as main story progress, their current rank, and weather. Party Member Social Links also tend to be unavailable if the current dungeon hasn't been completed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "activities",
      "title": "Activities",
      "intro_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section covers everything important found outside of dungeons that doesn't get elaborated on anywhere else in the guide. Because of the amount of content in this game, some smaller activities won't be covered here as they are usually self explanatory. Hopefully if you can't find something anywhere else, you can find it here."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "skill-list",
      "title": "Skill List"
    },
    {
      "id": "item-list",
      "title": "Item List",
      "intro_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "This section lists every item, what it does, where to find them, and any other relevant info necessary. More details for some items can be found in their respective sections elsewhere in this guide. Any item that is located at Hollow Forest can only be used in that dungeon, and cannot be used elsewhere."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tips-and-tricks",
      "title": "Tips And Tricks"
    },
    {
      "id": "conclusion",
      "title": "Conclusion"
    }
  ],
